; `Option`, consumed - the other half of the outcome types.
;
; `Option` is a compiler builtin, so it has no defining module, and
; until 2026-09-03 the standard library shipped ZERO ways to read one
; while fourteen public functions across `Str`, `Vec`, `Intern`,
; `Utf8` and `Path` answered one. Every caller hand-wrote the same
; four-line `match`, including callers inside `stdlib/Err.ax` a few
; lines above where these now live.
;
; They are in `Err.ax` beside `okOr` and `toOption` because that file
; already holds the two outcome types together, and a user who has an
; `(Option a)` out of `vecTry` should not have to know which of two
; modules names the thing that reads it.
;
; What each term establishes:
;
;   1. `isSome`/`isNone` on both cases, and that they DISAGREE - two
;      functions that both answered `true` would pass a test that only
;      checked one arm each.
;   2. `optUnwrapOr` takes the value when there is one and the
;      fallback when there is not, AND a stored zero is not an
;      absence: `(Some 0)` unwraps to 0 rather than to the fallback,
;      which is the whole reason `Option` is a type rather than a
;      sentinel. `tests/stdlib/313-vec-try.ax` pins the same
;      distinction on the producing side.
;   3. `optMap` applies over `Some`, passes `None` through, and
;      CHANGES THE TYPE: `(Option Int)` to `(Option String)`, which is
;      the signature's `b` doing work rather than decorating it.
;   4. `optAndThen` chains a function that can itself answer `None`,
;      in all three combinations - present-then-present,
;      present-then-absent, absent.
;   5. `optOr` takes the first present of two, and is NOT lazy: its
;      own comment says the alternative is evaluated at the call, and
;      the term is written so that a lazy implementation would print
;      something different.
;   6. THEY COMPOSE WITH A REAL PRODUCER. `strFind` answers
;      `(Option Int)`; the whole pipeline runs without a `match` at the
;      call site, which is the DX claim this file is the evidence for.
(import IO)

(import Err)

(import Str)

(import Vec)

(:: doubleIt (-> Int (Option Int)))

(fn (doubleIt n)
  (if (> n 100)
    None
    (Some (* n 2))
  )
)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let (
    (some7 (Some 7))
    (some0 (Some 0))
    (none0 None)
  )
    {
      ; --- 1. isSome and isNone, on both cases, disagreeing ---
      (println (isSome some7))
      (println (isNone some7))
      (println (isSome none0))
      (println (isNone none0))

      ; --- 2. optUnwrapOr, and Some 0 is not an absence ---
      (println (optUnwrapOr some7 99))
      (println (optUnwrapOr none0 99))
      (println (optUnwrapOr some0 99))

      ; --- 3. optMap, including a change of type ---
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optMap some7 (lambda (x) (* x 3))) 0))
      (println (isNone (optMap none0 (lambda (x) (* x 3)))))
      (println (optUnwrapOr
        (optMap some7 (lambda (x) (strConcat "n=" (fmtInt x))))        "none"
      ))

      ; --- 4. optAndThen, all three combinations ---
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optAndThen some7 doubleIt) 0))
      (println (isNone (optAndThen (Some 500) doubleIt)))
      (println (isNone (optAndThen none0 doubleIt)))

      ; --- 5. optOr takes the first present of two ---
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optOr some7 (Some 42)) 0))
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optOr none0 (Some 42)) 0))
      (println (isNone (optOr none0 None)))

      ; --- 6. composing with a real producer, no match at the call ---
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optMap (strFind "hello world" "world" 0) (lambda (i) (+ i 1))) 0))
      (println (optUnwrapOr (optMap (strFind "hello world" "zebra" 0) (lambda (i) (+ i 1))) 0))
      0
    }))
